    "title": "One hurt in rollover crash in Morton County - NewsBreak",
    "text": "MORTON COUNTY, Kan. (KSNW) — A Rolla man was seriously injured Wednesday evening in a rollover crash northeast of town. The Kansas Highway Patrol said the crash happened around 5:30 p.m. on County Road 26, about five miles northeast of Rolla. Troopers say that a northbound 2006 Ford Fusion lost control and rolled into a field before coming to rest upright. The driver, a 49-year-old man, was taken to a local hospital with suspected serious injuries. For more Kansas news, click here . Keep up with the latest breaking news by downloading our mobile app and signing up for our news email alerts . Sign up for our Storm Track 3 Weather app by clicking here . To watch our shows live on our website, click here. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KSN-TV.",
